          "code": "SUMMARY",
          "id": "1776914962985",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776914962985_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate a concise summary based on {{$context.$nodes.GET_RENEWAL_ACCOUNTS.$output}}. Exclude any raw data,\nidentifiers, or technical details. Focus only on the key insights and relevant information that provide a\nclear understanding of the renewal accounts."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7437.5,
            "y": 6592
          }
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_WIDGET",
          "id": "1776915660007",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776915660007_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Create an oraInfoDisplay multiRecordWidget from this normalized product-risk summary:\n{{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_RISK_SUMMARY.$output.result.items}}\n\nSet the widget title exactly to:\n\"Renewal Accounts\"\n\nSet the description to a polished 2-3 sentence executive paragraph based on {{$context.$nodes.GET_RENEWAL_ACCOUNTS.$output}} and appContext.\n\nProduct name rule:\n- Use appContext.targetProductName as the product display name.\n- If appContext is URL-encoded, decode it first and read targetProductName.\n- Never use targetProductId as the product name.\n- Never display values that look like IDs, such as strings starting with \"FUSION_\" or numeric identifiers.\n- If targetProductName is missing, use \"the target product\" instead of an ID.\n\nDescription requirements:\n- Write original executive-facing prose. Do not copy or repeat wording from these instructions.\n- Sentence 1 must start with \"Upcoming\" and describe the renewal opportunity as timely, strategic, and connected to business outcomes or long-term customer priorities. It must also mention the targetProduct {{$context.$variables.targetProductName}}.\n- Sentence 2 must start with \"Position [product display name]...\" and frame the product as a strategic investment supporting operational efficiency, compliance, adoption, productivity, customer value, or measurable business outcomes.\n- Sentence 3 must start with \"Target renewal conversations...\" and recommend messaging focused on retention, realized value, adoption maturity, expansion potential, and future growth.\n- Keep the tone professional, concise, executive-facing, and action-oriented.\n- Do not use generic phrases like \"maximize renewal success\", \"based on the data\", \"the table shows\", or \"accounts across risk segments\".\n- Do not mention raw data, account IDs, internal node names, JSON, APIs, product IDs, or technical details.\n- Write one natural paragraph, not bullets.\n\nDisplay exactly three data columns, in this order:\n- \"Product Risk\": Use the productRisk value. Display exactly four rows and exactly these labels: Critical, High, Medium, Stable.\n- \"# of Accounts\": Use the accounts value.\n- \"ARR Impact\": Use the arr value. It is already formatted with K for thousands, M for millions, B for billions, exactly two decimal places, and no space before the suffix.\n\nDo not create a separate data column named \"Action\". The action controls must render only as row actions/buttons, not as an additional table column without buttons.\n\nRows:\n- Include exactly these product risk groups, in this order: Critical, High, Medium, Stable.\n- Do not include or display At Risk, Moderate, Low, 180 Day Renewal Window, or Accounts as product-risk labels or column names.\n- If any source row uses Moderate, treat it as Medium and display Medium.\n\nFor every row, create exactly one row action button:\n{\n  \"text\": \"Send for Review\",\n  \"command\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"showRiskAccounts\\\",\\\"showRiskAccounts({\\\\\\\"accountType\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"<ProductRisk>\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pageNumber\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pageSize\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{{$context.$variables.accountDisplayPageSize}}\\\\\\\"})\\\")\"\n}\n\nReplace <ProductRisk> with the exact Product Risk value for that row: Critical, High, Medium, or Stable.\n\nReturn only the oraInfoDisplay widget. Do not include raw data, identifiers, explanations, markdown, or technical details outside the widget."
            },
            {
              "id": "1776915660007_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Output must follow multiRecordWidget patterns and actionable insights. Render Send for Review as row actions only; do not create a duplicate Action data column."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7887.5,
            "y": 6592
